        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How do I reset a Bowflex treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For a hung console, switch off, unplug at the wall and wait at least a minute (the T6 manual says 60 seconds), then power back on and insert the safety key. On the T6, holding STOP for 3 seconds only ends the workout and resets the display. Full console resets differ by model, so use the procedure in your own manual or ask support.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why will my Bowflex treadmill not turn on?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Check the outlet with a lamp, then that the treadmill is on a dedicated 15-amp circuit with no GFCI outlet, power strip, surge protector or extension cord, as the T6 manual requires. Confirm the cord is in at both ends and the power switch is on. If the switch lights but the console does not, the console cable is the next thing to check.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why does my Bowflex treadmill belt slip?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Usually because the belt has stretched or the deck needs silicone. On a T6, turn both rear roller bolts a quarter-turn clockwise with the belt stopped, test, and repeat until the slip goes, never more than a quarter-turn at a time. If lubrication is due, do that first, because tightening a belt over a dry deck makes the motor work harder.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How often should I lubricate a Bowflex treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The T6 manual says every three months or 150 miles, using 100% silicone, and the treadmill shows LUBE BELT and will not run until you deal with it. The older Treadmill 7 and 18 manual says every three months or 25 hours, whichever comes first. Never use petroleum-based products or WD-40.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why will my Bowflex treadmill not connect to JRNY?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On the T6 and T9, JRNY runs on your phone or tablet. Turn on both Bluetooth and Location, open the BowFlex JRNY app close to the treadmill and follow its sync steps. If it still will not sync, restart your device and the treadmill and try again; the T6 manual gives exactly that sequence.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Who makes Bowflex treadmills now?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Johnson Health Tech bought the BowFlex brand and assets out of bankruptcy in 2024, and bowflex.com now carries a Johnson Health Tech Trading copyright line. Before that, Bowflex treadmills were made by Nautilus, Inc. Owners of older Nautilus-era machines should ask support what cover applies to them.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where is the serial number on a Bowflex treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On the T6, the manual says it is on a white barcode sticker near the on/off power switch and the power cord. Write it and the model name in the front of your manual, because support asks for both along with proof of purchase.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
          <div class="author-card">
            <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="56" height="56" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <div class="ac-k">Written by</div>
